# LF everywhere. Without this, a checkout on Windows converts text files to
# CRLF, and hooks/bootstrap.sh — the documented install path, which WSL2 users
# reach via a Windows checkout — fails to parse at all:
#
#   bootstrap.sh: line 21: syntax error near unexpected token `$'in\r''
#
# Committed rather than left to each developer's global config so the
# convention travels with the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and the graph DB are unambiguous: never let them be rewritten.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.db binary
